## 🛠️ Setup & Deployment

### 1. Clone the repo
```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/forex-trading-bot.git
cd forex-trading-bot
```

### 2. Install dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 3. Configure environment variables
Create a `.env` file:
```env
CAPITAL_API_KEY=your_api_key
CAPITAL_IDENTIFIER=your_email
CAPITAL_PASSWORD=your_password
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your_bot_token
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=your_chat_id
ENVIRONMENT=demo  # or live
```

### 4. Run the bot
```bash
python strategy_v1.py
```

### 5. Run the dashboard
```bash
python dashboard_server.py
```

---

## ☁️ Cloud Deployment (Railway)

The bot is deployed on [Railway](https://railway.app) with automatic GitHub integration:

1. Push to `main` branch → Railway auto-deploys
2. Set environment variables in Railway dashboard
3. Bot runs 24/7 with automatic restarts

---

## 🔧 Known API Quirks Solved

| Issue | Fix Applied |
|-------|------------|
| TP silently rejected | All float values cast with `float()` to avoid numpy float64 rejection |
| SL moving not supported via API | Bot-managed SL logic implemented in Python |
| `dealId` vs `dealReference` confusion | Correct field (`affectedDeals` dealId) used for all modifications |
| 429 rate limit errors | Sleep delays added between API calls |
| SL "maxvalue" errors | Pip buffer added while tracking exact TP1 internally |

